          cushioning system and delivers a nearly identical day-to-day
          experience for walkers and moderate joggers at $500 less. The jump
          to the <a href="/nordictrack-commercial-2950-treadmill">Commercial 2950</a>
          buys a further-stronger 4.5 CHP motor and a much larger 32-inch
          screen, but for roughly $1,700-$2,200 more — a price most runners,
          even serious ones, will struggle to justify once they've already
          got the 2450's incline ceiling and motor reserve.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you're comparing across brands rather than just within
          NordicTrack's own lineup, our
          <a href="/commercial-treadmills">commercial treadmill roundup</a>
          covers competing flagship and near-flagship machines at similar
          price points, some of which prioritize deck size or console
