              Yes, this is where the 2450 earns its price most clearly. The
              15% max incline is steep enough for genuinely demanding
              simulated climbs, and the stronger motor keeps belt speed
              consistent even during sustained incline work, which is
              exactly the scenario where the 1750's smaller motor starts to
              feel like it's working harder than it should.
            </p>
          </div>
