              The 2950 adds a stronger 4.5 CHP motor and a much larger
              32-inch touchscreen for roughly $1,700-$2,200 more, while
              incline range, deck size, and cushioning stay the same. Most
              runners, including serious ones, won't feel a meaningful
              difference in daily use between the two motors, which makes
              the 2450 the better value for all but the most dedicated
              buyers.
            </p>
